_help() {
  cat << EOF
$(_version) - Universal package manager bootstrap installer

USAGE:
    # Script manager interface (called by pkgman)
    $__APP <action> <manager> [--dest=<path>] [--artifact=<name>]
    
    # Independent execution
    $__APP [OPTIONS] <action> [manager]

ACTIONS:
    install <manager>    Install/provision the specified package manager
    update <manager>     Update the specified package manager  
    uninstall <manager>  Remove the package manager (not supported - prevents deprovisioning)
    status <manager>     Check if package manager is installed (returns: installed/missing)
    help [manager]       Show help for specific manager or general help

OPTIONS:
    -h                   Show this help
    -v                   Show version

SUPPORTED MANAGERS:
    brew                 Homebrew package manager (manual installation)
    apt                  APT package manager (system dependency)
    dnf                  DNF package manager (system dependency)  
    mas                  Mac App Store CLI (dogfooding via brew)
    cargo                Rust package manager (dogfooding via brew)
    go                   Go programming language (dogfooding, OS-specific)
    pipx                 Python application installer (dogfooding)
    npm                  Node.js package manager (dogfooding)
    download             Download manager (utility - validates curl/wget)
    github               GitHub manager (utility - validates GitHub API access)
    script               Script manager (utility - validates bash availability)

BOOTSTRAP STRATEGY:
    1. Manual Installation: brew (foundation package manager)
    2. Dogfooding: mas, cargo, go, pipx, npm installed via pkgman using brew
    3. System Dependencies: apt/dnf assumed pre-installed on respective systems
    4. Utility Managers: download, github, script validate system dependencies

EXAMPLES:
    # Script manager interface
    $__APP install brew
    $__APP status mas
    
    # Independent execution
    $__APP install cargo
    $__APP help go
    $__APP status npm

INTEGRATION:
    This script complies with pkgman script manager interface while supporting
    independent execution. It's designed to be called by pkgman's script manager
    but can also be run directly for manual bootstrapping.

NOTES:
    - Uninstall operations are not supported to prevent system deprovisioning
    - Uses pkgman dogfooding approach where possible for consistency
    - brew installation is manual (foundation for other installations)
    - System package managers (apt/dnf) are assumed to be pre-installed
EOF
}

